SUMMARY:ARC Ensemble:  Artists of the Royal Conservatory ($40)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n{ This concert is SOLD-OUT }\n\nThe **
 ARC Ensemble** and students of the **Glenn Gould School** explore ***Armen
 ian works composed*** before the breakup of the Soviet Union and Armenian 
 independence – captivating and evocative music unknown in the West. Incl
 uded on the program are arrangements of Armenian folksongs for string quar
 tet\, a compelling Cello Sonata by Avet Terteryan\, and seductive piano mi
 niatures by Alexander Spendiarian and Arno Babadjanian.\n\n**Ticket link i
 s below**\\-\\-\\-and\\-\\-\\-ANY seat is a great seat\\.\n\nhttps://bit.l
 y/ARCConcertOct4\n\nThe multiple Grammy Award nominated ARC Ensemble compr
 ises the senior faculty of The Royal Conservatory's Glenn Gould School\, w
 ith special guests drawn from the organization's most accomplished student
 s and alumni. **It is among Canada's most distinguished cultural ambassado
 rs** with recent appearances in Los Angeles\, New York and London’s Wigm
 ore Hall. The research and recovery of music suppressed and marginalized u
 nder the 20th century's repressive regimes remains its focus and a growing
  number of works have now rejoined the repertoire.\n“As always with this
  ensemble\, performances could hardly be bettered in terms of execution an
 d commitment.” (*Gramophone*)\n\n**ARC Ensemble-**\n**(Artists of The Ro
 yal Conservatory)**\n\n**Erika Raum**\, violin\n**Marie Bérard**\, violin
 \n**Steven Dann**\, viola\n**Thomas Wiebe**\, cello\n**Kevin Ahfat**\, pia
 no\n\nwith students of **The Glenn Gould School-**\n\n**Avery Tracy**\, vi
 olin\n**Gina Lanzrein**\, violin\n**Shyler Macaggi**\, viola\n**Mira Karda
 n**\, cello\n\n**TICKET Link here:**\n\nhttps://www.rcmusic.com/concert/ar
 c-ensemble-453001?utm_source=meetup&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=45300
 1_ARCconcert&utm_content=arts_events_listing
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31577
 6820/
